  "notes": "University Park. Major code 'MATSCI' avoids colliding with the MATSE department prefix. Historical-year build (2026-09-17), fetched the real archived bulletin at the URL in 'source' above (raw HTML via curl, cross-checked against the page's own printed semester/fall/spring subtotals and 'minimum of 131 credits' program-requirements total, not WebFetch's summary) and compared it course-by-course against MATSCI-2026.json's already-verified structure. Course-by-course identical to the 2022 archived bulletin (both use the same real Processing Laboratory numbering MATSE 463/468/472/474 and the same two unresolved 'MATSE 448'/'MATSE 444' elective entries described below), and structurally identical to 2026 in every other respect: same 131-credit minimum, same full Prescribed/Additional Courses list including MATSE 436 and the Processing Laboratory requirement (both real required items on this year's bulletin already, same as every other year checked), same Entrance-to-Major requirements, same 12-credit Technical Elective pool, and the same real CHEM 110 -> MATH 22/21/4/3 prereq chain (re-verified for 2022, the adjacent archived edition, directly against its own archived MATH/CHEM course-description pages -- wording identical to the current catalog) -- so this file carries over the 2026 plan's MATH 3/4/21/22 additions and its 21-credit/semester cap unchanged. (1) Processing Laboratory: this year's page prints MATSE 463, MATSE 468, and two plain-text/non-hyperlinked entries 'MATSE 472' and 'MATSE 474' (verified present at byte level in the raw archived HTML) -- current 2026 numbering (471/473) is absent from this year's page entirely. Used MATSE 463/468/472/474 here to match. (2) The 'Synthesis and Processing' list additionally prints an unresolved 'MATSE 448' beyond its 5 standard options, and 'Structure and Characterization' an unresolved 'MATSE 444' beyond its 5 -- neither resolves to a title/credit value on this year's own bulletin page and neither is in this app's scraped MATSE catalog, so neither was added to the MATSE Specialization Course match regex (kept at 2026's 5-per-category list); flagged here rather than silently dropped. (3) A genuine internal inconsistency on THIS year's own page: the Suggested Academic Plan's Second Year Fall row prints MATH 220's credits as '3' (making that semester's own stated subtotal 18), but this SAME page's Program Requirements Course List explicitly lists MATH 220 ('Matrices') as 2 credits -- matching every other year checked (2022, 2024, 2025, 2026 all show 2 credits for MATH 220, both in their course lists and in 2022's suggested-plan row). Treated the '3' as a bulletin data-entry error specific to this year's Suggested Academic Plan table and kept MATH 220 at its real 2 credits in this file, rather than propagating a phantom extra credit. Sequencing note (observed, not applied): same as the 2022 file -- this year's own Suggested Academic Plan places both 'IE 424 or STAT 401' and 'MATSE 413' in Second Year Spring (this file's Semester 4), not Semester 6/7 as in the 2026 JSON. Kept this file's placement identical to 2026's (Semester 6 / Semester 7) for the same reasons given in the 2022 file's notes: no tracked prerequisite on either course, 0 scheduling warnings either way, and the 2026 file's placement is already a deliberate credit-cap rearrangement, not a literal per-year bulletin mirror.",
